  "abstract_summary": "Context. Ultraluminous X-ray sources (ULXs) are thought to be powered, in many cases, by super-Eddington accretion onto compact objects. While soft X-ray lags have been detected in several ULXs, hard lags remain rare and poorly understood. Aims. We investigate the temporal and energy dependence of X-ray lags in NGC...",
